WEBVTT

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:04.060
Shiseido Parlour?

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:05.000
Yeah.

00:00:05.000 --> 00:00:11.840
My friend said they saw you there 
with an incredibly handsome foreigner.

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.120
Oh, that's Richard. My boss.

00:00:15.120 --> 00:00:16.690
Oh, the jeweler?

00:00:16.690 --> 00:00:17.490
Yeah.

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:22.460
It's like having a nice 
older brother. It's great.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:23.680
Sounds nice.

00:00:23.680 --> 00:00:26.760
I had someone like that when I was little.

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:30.470
Our parents were friends. 
He played with me a lot.

00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:35.790
You don't say! My older brother figure 
was my senpai in karate class.

00:00:36.870 --> 00:00:42.180
When I lost my final match in middle school, 
he said he'd avenge me.

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.650
He was so cool.

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:47.180
He was so strong, we all called 
him the King of Destruction.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.440
I really looked up to him.

00:00:49.440 --> 00:00:51.710
You did karate, Seigi-kun?

00:00:51.710 --> 00:00:52.440
Huh?

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.950
Oh, yeah. Through middle school.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:58.120
Wow, that's amazing. Can you still do it?

00:00:59.430 --> 00:01:00.320
Yeah.

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:05.370
This was my senpai's special move.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:11.880
Are you okay, Seigi-kun?

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:50.020
<u>Episode 5</u>
<b>Opal of Encounters</b>

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:54.770
I see.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:03:00.700
So you pulled your back while recklessly 
attempting a spinning high kick.

00:03:01.030 --> 00:03:05.470
Aw, man... I embarrassed myself 
in front of Tanimoto-san.

00:03:05.470 --> 00:03:06.450
Tanimoto-san?

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:09.660
Oh, um... She's a friend from college.

00:03:10.460 --> 00:03:13.420
I see. She's your girlfriend.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:15.920
What?! No, not yet!

00:03:16.260 --> 00:03:17.780
Ow...

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:22.630
Anyway, wasn't my senpai the coolest?

00:03:22.630 --> 00:03:26.430
He even said he avenged me!

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:30.180
I wonder what he's doing now.

00:03:30.490 --> 00:03:36.380
I mean, I haven't seen him since 
we quit learning karate.

00:03:36.960 --> 00:03:40.200
In this life, we sometimes 
have chance encounters

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:43.070
with people we strongly wish to see.

00:03:43.380 --> 00:03:45.130
Chance encounters, huh?

00:03:48.020 --> 00:03:51.510
Our client should be arriving 
for their appointment soon.

00:03:51.510 --> 00:03:53.270
Please prepare for their arrival.

00:03:53.270 --> 00:03:54.360
Got it.

00:03:56.630 --> 00:03:59.210
<b>Shinbashi Station</b>

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:02.130
<b>Time</b>

00:03:59.210 --> 00:04:02.130
<b>Temp</b>

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:12.210
Excuse me.

00:04:13.060 --> 00:04:14.070
Huh?

00:04:15.270 --> 00:04:17.420
Hase-senpai?

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:18.690
Is that you, Seigi?

00:04:19.370 --> 00:04:20.490
Yeah!

00:04:20.490 --> 00:04:22.720
Wow, what a blast from the past!

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:24.210
How many years has it been?

00:04:24.210 --> 00:04:26.030
That hurts, Senpai!

00:04:26.030 --> 00:04:27.740
Cheers!

00:04:31.210 --> 00:04:32.250
That's good stuff!

00:04:32.250 --> 00:04:34.750
But, man, you really surprised me.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:37.690
I thought you'd gone off to college.

00:04:39.570 --> 00:04:44.090
For family reasons, 
I dropped out last year and got a job.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:46.400
I'm in operations now.

00:04:46.400 --> 00:04:49.390
I see. Sounds rough.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:54.060
Let's not talk about depressing stuff.
 Come on, eat.

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:55.890
It's on me.

00:04:57.270 --> 00:04:59.290
Thanks, Senpai!

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:06.280
It's not that funny.

00:05:06.280 --> 00:05:11.230
But the former King of Destruction
 is a rabbit now.

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.370
We had a small fire at the office.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:18.830
After I helped an employee in a wheelchair, 
she started calling me "Rabbit."

00:05:19.100 --> 00:05:20.970
What? But why?

00:05:20.970 --> 00:05:23.170
I have no idea.

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:27.090
Anyway, how about you? 
What's new with you?

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:30.800
My grandma passed away.

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:32.880
Your grandma?

00:05:35.850 --> 00:05:39.860
So the real owner of your 
grandma's ring was still alive?

00:05:39.860 --> 00:05:42.570
Yeah. I was surprised, too.

00:05:42.570 --> 00:05:44.310
What did you do?

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:46.990
I went to Kobe to return it.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:52.130
But she said she wanted me to have it.

00:05:52.550 --> 00:05:54.290
You didn't get to return it?

00:05:54.290 --> 00:05:55.450
No.

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:58.850
I bet it's worth a pretty penny if you sell it.

00:05:58.850 --> 00:06:01.290
Grandma would be furious with me.

00:06:02.620 --> 00:06:07.030
The jeweler who found the owner 
is pretty impressive, too.

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:07.840
Yeah.

00:06:08.400 --> 00:06:10.250
A jeweler, huh?

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:13.540
What about jewelers?

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:17.540
Oh, it's just that I've been looking for one.

00:06:17.540 --> 00:06:20.890
Senpai, could it be... 
Are you getting married?!

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.280
Keep your voice down!

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:25.090
Congratulations!

00:06:25.090 --> 00:06:27.030
It's not like that.

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:30.600
Can we get dinner again next week?

00:06:30.600 --> 00:06:32.500
Of course.

00:06:32.500 --> 00:06:34.220
In that case, see you then.

00:06:34.220 --> 00:06:36.190
Yeah. See you next week.

00:06:39.560 --> 00:06:42.000
Chance encounters, huh?

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:52.460
Did something good happen?

00:06:52.800 --> 00:06:53.680
Yeah.

00:06:55.260 --> 00:06:58.890
But just so you know, it has nothing 
to do with Tanimoto-san.

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:03.020
Last week, on my way home from work, 
I happened to run into my senpai.

00:07:03.390 --> 00:07:04.860
From karate class?

00:07:04.860 --> 00:07:08.600
Yeah. He hasn't changed at all.

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:12.360
<b>Housing Information</b>

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:12.360
<b>Choosing a home for everyone</b>

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:12.360
<b>No. 1 with the most listings!</b>

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:12.360
<b>Tokyo Metro</b>

00:07:09.860 --> 00:07:12.360
<b>New Apartment Special Issue</b>

00:07:12.360 --> 00:07:13.720
What's this?

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:17.830
Oh, he's getting married soon.

00:07:17.830 --> 00:07:20.940
I want to help him in any way I can.

00:07:21.500 --> 00:07:22.460
Seigi.

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:28.660
I'm very familiar with how much 
of a busybody you can be,

00:07:28.660 --> 00:07:31.010
but perhaps you should restrain yourself.

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:32.970
I know, I know.

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:36.960
But he's always done things for me.

00:07:36.960 --> 00:07:39.150
I want to do something to pay him back.

00:07:41.800 --> 00:07:43.260
I'll answer it.

00:07:49.400 --> 00:07:52.370
Welcome to Étranger.

00:07:52.370 --> 00:07:56.280
Er, thank you. This is a jeweler's, right?

00:07:56.280 --> 00:07:58.050
Indeed.

00:07:58.050 --> 00:07:59.290
It's him!

00:07:59.290 --> 00:08:02.620
I came to discuss a sale. 
Could you take a look?

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:04.370
A sale?

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:07.930
We don't specialize in purchases.

00:08:07.930 --> 00:08:10.130
If you could just take a look...

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:19.510
This appears to be a fire opal.

00:08:19.510 --> 00:08:23.410
Yes. My grandmother gave it to me,

00:08:23.410 --> 00:08:26.610
but she's passed away.

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:31.850
I was actually lucky enough to be able
 to find the stone's original owner.

00:08:31.850 --> 00:08:36.740
I even went to return it, 
but they wouldn't accept it.

00:08:36.740 --> 00:08:40.720
They said they wanted me to hold on to it.

00:08:40.720 --> 00:08:42.440
Strange, right?

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:46.920
Why is he telling my story?

00:08:47.220 --> 00:08:50.210
That certainly is a strange turn of events.

00:08:50.860 --> 00:08:56.290
I apologize for the intrusive question, 
but where does said owner live?

00:08:56.290 --> 00:08:59.810
Uh... Kobe. Yeah, in Kobe.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:02.270
If you don't mind,

00:09:02.550 --> 00:09:07.070
could you please tell me the name 
of the person who referred you here?

00:09:08.230 --> 00:09:10.590
If you can't buy it, that's fine.

00:09:10.590 --> 00:09:11.780
I'll go someplace else.

00:09:23.410 --> 00:09:26.120
Sorry I took so long.

00:09:26.120 --> 00:09:29.390
Please try to be quicker next time.

00:09:29.390 --> 00:09:30.670
Understood.

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:38.010
<b>Time</b>

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:38.010
<b>Temp</b>

00:09:43.470 --> 00:09:45.480
Hey, sorry to keep you waiting.

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:51.480
You seem down. Is the meat 
too heavy on your stomach?

00:09:52.010 --> 00:09:55.740
Senpai, is there something troubling you?

00:09:57.150 --> 00:10:00.280
Still playing the hero of justice, huh?

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:05.850
You haven't changed since middle school.

00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:08.630
So there's nothing troubling you?

00:10:08.630 --> 00:10:10.000
Well...

00:10:10.380 --> 00:10:12.130
Do you know what a "kainoshi" is?

00:10:12.620 --> 00:10:15.380
"Kainoshi"? What's that?

00:10:15.380 --> 00:10:18.260
If you don't, then never mind.

00:10:19.340 --> 00:10:20.260
Senpai...

00:10:21.570 --> 00:10:23.900
Why don't we split the check today?

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:27.140
What? Don't get ahead of yourself, student.

00:10:27.400 --> 00:10:29.120
Come on. Eat up.

00:10:38.430 --> 00:10:40.570
I avenged you.

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:54.290
<b>Display</b>

00:10:49.080 --> 00:10:54.290
<b>Menu</b>

00:10:49.900 --> 00:10:52.820
She doesn't have an appointment.

00:10:52.820 --> 00:10:54.290
That's fine.

00:10:55.550 --> 00:10:58.940
Welcome to Étranger.

00:10:58.940 --> 00:11:01.190
Pardon me for asking,

00:11:01.190 --> 00:11:05.640
but has anyone been here recently 
trying to sell you an opal?

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:06.530
What?

00:11:06.530 --> 00:11:11.060
An opal about this size 
that's a mix of orange and red.

00:11:12.330 --> 00:11:14.500
He was here, wasn't he?

00:11:14.970 --> 00:11:19.440
I'm sorry. We can't share personal 
information about our customers.

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:21.350
It belongs to my aunt!

00:11:21.350 --> 00:11:23.160
Hase-san stole it!

00:11:30.780 --> 00:11:33.000
My name is Hata.

00:11:33.540 --> 00:11:41.090
Hase-san takes care of my aunt, 
Sugano Hisa, at a nursing facility.

00:11:41.090 --> 00:11:43.530
He doesn't work in operations?

00:11:43.530 --> 00:11:45.810
No. He's on the nursing staff.

00:11:46.500 --> 00:11:47.920
I see.

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:50.100
Please continue.

00:11:50.710 --> 00:11:57.350
My aunt has mild dementia. 
Sometimes she doesn't even recognize me.

00:11:57.350 --> 00:12:02.390
But she calls Hase-san "Rabbit" 
and loves him dearly.

00:12:02.860 --> 00:12:04.850
There was a small fire at the home,

00:12:04.850 --> 00:12:09.230
and Hase-san carried my disabled 
aunt out of the building.

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:11.120
Rabbit...

00:12:11.740 --> 00:12:16.380
<i>After I helped an employee in a wheelchair, 
they started calling me "Rabbit."</i>

00:12:17.030 --> 00:12:23.130
It was after the fire that I noticed 
my aunt's opal was missing.

00:12:23.400 --> 00:12:26.890
Hase-san insists that she gave it to him.

00:12:26.890 --> 00:12:33.050
But my uncle gave that opal to my aunt
for their golden wedding anniversary.

00:12:35.830 --> 00:12:41.270
If Hase-san comes again, 
please tell him to contact me.

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:52.240
My senpai was looking for a wedding ring, 
so I referred him to Étranger.

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:54.000
I'm sorry I didn't say anything.

00:12:54.550 --> 00:12:57.950
I wish you had told me then.

00:12:58.520 --> 00:13:02.700
You're right. I'm sorry.

00:13:11.170 --> 00:13:14.240
Welcome to Étranger.

00:13:14.240 --> 00:13:17.020
Thanks. I'd like you to take another look.

00:13:20.790 --> 00:13:25.650
As I told you before, we don't 
specialize in purchasing gemstones here.

00:13:25.980 --> 00:13:28.710
Moreover, there are some things we can't buy.

00:13:28.710 --> 00:13:29.700
Can't buy?

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:34.120
For example, potentially stolen goods.

00:13:36.040 --> 00:13:38.040
You think I stole it?

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:41.710
You look down on me because 
I'm Japanese, don't you?

00:13:41.710 --> 00:13:47.000
This place looks like some tourist trap. 
I bet it's unlicensed, isn't it?

00:13:47.930 --> 00:13:51.080
You know, I used to practice karate.

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:53.300
They called me the King of Destruction.

00:13:57.220 --> 00:13:58.430
Senpai.

00:14:02.220 --> 00:14:05.810
Seigi? What are you doing here?

00:14:06.210 --> 00:14:08.600
I work here.

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:09.520
What?

00:14:10.990 --> 00:14:14.660
Someone named Hata-san was here earlier.

00:14:15.430 --> 00:14:17.080
What was Hata-san doing here?

00:14:20.460 --> 00:14:23.930
She said I stole it, didn't she?

00:14:23.930 --> 00:14:25.430
You can't be serious!

00:14:25.430 --> 00:14:28.060
Hisa-san gave me this gemstone!

00:14:28.570 --> 00:14:32.480
I tried over and over to refuse, 
but she insisted I take it!

00:14:32.480 --> 00:14:34.340
She said it was a kainoshi!

00:14:34.810 --> 00:14:37.620
And I wasn't lying when I said 
she shared her concerns with me.

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:42.070
Hisa-san said she might run out 
of money to pay for her care.

00:14:42.070 --> 00:14:48.280
So... I thought I might be able to help 
if I sold the gemstone for funds.

00:14:49.470 --> 00:14:52.450
Then you were trying to help Hisa-san?

00:14:53.820 --> 00:14:55.450
Y-Yeah...

00:14:57.200 --> 00:15:00.190
You mentioned a "kainoshi."

00:15:00.190 --> 00:15:03.460
Does Hisa-sama have bad teeth?

00:15:03.460 --> 00:15:05.360
What? Yeah...

00:15:05.360 --> 00:15:08.800
She's missing a lot of them. 
She has difficulty talking.

00:15:09.680 --> 00:15:10.720
I see.

00:15:13.550 --> 00:15:18.430
Hase-sama, are you familiar with the 
Miyazawa Kenji story called "Kai-no-Hi"?

00:15:18.990 --> 00:15:20.230
"Kai-no-hi"?

00:15:20.230 --> 00:15:20.940
Yes.

00:15:21.610 --> 00:15:24.940
A rabbit who rescues a skylark 
from drowning in a river

00:15:24.940 --> 00:15:28.940
is given a gemstone called a kai-no-hi, 
or "fiery shell," as thanks.

00:15:29.900 --> 00:15:31.200
A rabbit...

00:15:31.500 --> 00:15:37.290
"Fiery shells" are what the mineral-loving 
Kenji called fire opals.

00:15:37.960 --> 00:15:42.040
The quality of a gemstone exhibiting 
a variety of colors in the light

00:15:42.040 --> 00:15:45.140
is known as opalescence.

00:15:45.700 --> 00:15:49.610
This one that glitters with the 
colors of flames and rainbows

00:15:49.610 --> 00:15:51.820
is a true "fiery shell."

00:15:52.300 --> 00:15:56.540
So it wasn't kainoshi, but kai-no-hi?

00:15:58.850 --> 00:16:02.120
Since Hisa-sama has dementia,

00:16:02.120 --> 00:16:07.430
I believe it would be best to confirm to 
what degree she is aware of the situation.

00:16:09.220 --> 00:16:13.570
Also, there's more to the "Kai-no-Hi" story. 
Are you familiar with it?

00:16:14.520 --> 00:16:15.640
No.

00:16:15.640 --> 00:16:19.920
When handled poorly, 
the gemstone loses its sparkle.

00:16:19.920 --> 00:16:21.240
Handled poorly?

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:22.080
Yes.

00:16:22.350 --> 00:16:26.710
The rabbit eats bread stolen 
by a fox, knowing it's stolen,

00:16:26.710 --> 00:16:30.940
and repays the skylark's 
generosity with harm.

00:16:32.560 --> 00:16:36.360
Then, one day, as though 
it were divine punishment,

00:16:36.360 --> 00:16:38.300
the stone suddenly lost its sparkle.

00:16:43.860 --> 00:16:49.820
It's truly strange, 
but I know of a very similar story...

00:16:50.260 --> 00:16:53.410
The story of your grandmother's gemstone.

00:16:56.520 --> 00:17:00.820
Were you here the last time I came?

00:17:04.530 --> 00:17:06.170
You're a jerk.

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:27.850
<b>Time</b>

00:17:24.350 --> 00:17:27.850
<b>Temp</b>

00:17:34.840 --> 00:17:36.280
Senpai...

00:17:36.670 --> 00:17:40.080
I returned the opal to Hata-san.

00:17:40.080 --> 00:17:41.640
I quit my job, too.

00:17:42.530 --> 00:17:47.240
Senpai, I'll tell Hata-san the truth.

00:17:47.240 --> 00:17:48.380
If I explain things—

00:17:48.380 --> 00:17:50.830
You really are a hero of justice, aren't you?

00:17:50.830 --> 00:17:51.630
Huh?

00:17:52.080 --> 00:17:56.090
My dad collapsed, 
and my sister's still in school.

00:17:56.090 --> 00:17:58.590
I only wanted to help my family out.

00:17:59.220 --> 00:18:02.100
Weren't you doing it for Hisa-san?

00:18:02.100 --> 00:18:04.610
You always do the right thing.

00:18:04.610 --> 00:18:08.770
But not everyone can be like you.

00:18:11.700 --> 00:18:15.520
Say, Seigi, do you remember that match?

00:18:15.520 --> 00:18:17.740
My last match in middle school?

00:18:18.220 --> 00:18:23.280
If I could only go back to that time 
when I was buying you dinner...

00:18:23.820 --> 00:18:26.860
I could be the cool senpai 
you admired again.

00:18:30.280 --> 00:18:31.870
Thanks for everything.

00:18:33.420 --> 00:18:37.090
But I don't want to see your face again.

00:18:37.090 --> 00:18:38.930
It hurts too much.

00:19:18.800 --> 00:19:22.960
Pardon me for asking, but do you
 have any plans after this?

00:19:23.360 --> 00:19:25.780
Richard... But how?

00:19:26.210 --> 00:19:28.100
I had nothing to do, so I went for a drive.

00:19:28.940 --> 00:19:31.850
Were you waiting for me?

00:19:32.740 --> 00:19:36.320
I'm feeling a bit hungry. 
Care to make it dinner for two?

00:19:51.570 --> 00:19:54.960
I'm no hero of justice.

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:58.670
I'm just afraid of disappointing people 
by not being able to do anything.

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:03.520
I'm not right at all.

00:20:07.260 --> 00:20:10.180
Those who try to be right are solitary.

00:20:10.580 --> 00:20:14.500
Not everyone can walk the same path,

00:20:15.190 --> 00:20:18.320
and people dislike that 
which shines too brightly.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:22.200
Nevertheless, you're not wrong.

00:20:24.240 --> 00:20:26.720
The root of your righteousness

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:30.760
is a noble desire to be kind 
to others even in the darkness.

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:37.170
I find that desire admirable, 
from the bottom of my heart.

00:20:37.890 --> 00:20:40.550
At times, I envy it.

00:20:58.510 --> 00:21:00.090
Pull yourself together.

00:21:28.220 --> 00:21:31.010
Chance encounters, huh?

00:21:31.910 --> 00:21:33.110
What is it?

00:21:33.110 --> 00:21:39.270
Nothing. I just wish I could send those 
drunks from back then a box of cakes.

00:21:40.060 --> 00:21:43.780
I wouldn't mind eating them instead.
